# Static UI copy — title case

Developer-authored labels (menus, form sections, buttons, settings rows, placeholders) use **title case**: capitalize the first letter of each word. Words are separated by spaces or `/`, `·`, or `-`.

Examples:
- `New budget` → `New Budget`
- `Lender / bank name` → `Lender / Bank Name`
- `Alert when exceeded` → `Alert When Exceeded`

**Do not** transform user-entered data (transaction notes, loan names, category names). Use `applyStaticLabelCaseToTitle = false` on `MmrTopAppBar` when the title is user content.

Implementation: `String.mmrStaticLabelCase()` in `com.rrparallelstudio.miapp.ui.copy.MmrStaticUiCopy`. Shared chrome (`MmrFormSectionLabel`, settings rows, form pickers, primary buttons, dialog titles) applies it at render time. New raw `Text("…")` labels in features should either use those components or call `mmrStaticLabelCase()` explicitly.

Sentence-style **messages** (dialog body, errors, footers) stay normal sentence case unless they are short labels.
